@startuml sequence-uc1
' System sequence diagram for UC-1 "Find a passage by question".
' The flow numbers match the use case in section 2.6 of ba.md.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam dpi 150

actor Reader
participant "Web client\n(Librarian panel)" as Client
participant "API\n(conversations)" as API
participant "librarian.py" as Lib
participant "rag.search" as Search
database "SQLite\n(chunks, FTS5,\nvectors)" as DB
participant "LLM API" as LLM

Reader -> Client : type a question, send
Client -> API : POST /api/conversations/{id}/messages
API -> DB : save the question
API -> Lib : generate_reply(question)
Lib -> LLM : ask for 5 descriptors of the question
alt the LLM answers
  LLM --> Lib : descriptors (JSON)
  Lib -> Search : search(question, configured method, k=3)
else no answer in 10 s (flow 3a)
  Lib -> Search : search(question, "bm25+dense", k=3)
end
Search -> DB : read BM25 scores, text vectors,\ndescriptor vectors
DB --> Search : scores for every chunk
Search --> Lib : top 3 chunks
alt passages found
  Lib --> API : passages (book, chapter, excerpt)
else nothing matches (flow 4a)
  Lib --> API : "no passage found"
end
API --> Client : stream the reply (Server-Sent Events)
API -> DB : save the reply
Client --> Reader : show the passages
Reader -> Client : select a passage
Client --> Reader : open the book at that chapter
@enduml
